# A bound function that is made in one function and called in a loop of another: out of a variable of the file, out of a parameter.
# Link writes what is seen in the place: BoundFunction<add, never, never>. The walk takes it for an expectation and asks the cell: a bound function . no bound argument . its target a closure of add: and enters add.
# A unit may mention only what its function names (LinkTables::mayBeMentionedBy): the reader of the place names the target that the type of the place writes, as it names a closure that the type writes.
